## Pin: B10 — non-generic classes (AtomicI64) keep their `.new -> Int`
## by default; the lift fires only when the lib decl declares an
## explicit structured return. AtomicI64's lib decl was changed to
## return `AtomicI64`, so this typechecks. The negative half is
## checked indirectly: if a Plain class were declared with `-> Int`
## and no structured override, typeck would report Int (no field).
def main
  let a = AtomicI64.new(0)
  let _prev = a.fetch_add(5)
  let _cur = a.load
end
